OL,3,GNEWSAUnder-16s could be banned from
OL,4,Abuying energy drinks in Wales
OL,5,
OL,6,FYoung people and experts say they
OL,7,Fsupport the Welsh government's plan to
OL,8,Fban children under 16 from buying
OL,9,Fhigh-caffeine energy drinks.
OL,11,FThe Welsh government said that evidence
OL,12,Fsuggests a link between "consumption of
OL,13,Fhigh-caffeine energy drinks and
OL,14,Fnegative health outcomes", and is
OL,15,Fconsidering a ban on under 16s buying
OL,16,Fthem.
OL,18,FBBC Wales spoke to young people in
OL,19,FCardiff who said they supported the
OL,20,Fproposed ban, with one 17-year-old
OL,21,Fsaying it was "really easy to start
OL,22,Frelying on them".
OL,23,APub: 06-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
